# Cursor / Assistant Rules: Anti-AI Slop & Apple/iOS Design System
# Applied to IRIS & Universal Projects

# 1. CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY
- You MUST adhere strictly to the guidelines defined in ANTI_AI_SLOP.md.
- Adopt Apple / iOS 18 / macOS Sequoia design language:
  - Frosted glass materials (backdrop-blur-xl, translucent surfaces).
  - Continuous squircles (rounded-2xl, rounded-3xl).
  - Subtle 1px borders (border-black/[0.06] or border-white/[0.1]).
  - Multi-stop ambient shadows, never muddy pitch-black shadows.
  - Apple-style segmented controls for filters and tabs.
  - Tactile micro-interactions (active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-150).
  - Clean San Francisco / Inter typography with tabular numbers (font-mono tabular-nums).

# 2. PROHIBITED AI TROPES (NEVER DO THIS)
- NO purple-pink AI gradients (from-purple-600 to-pink-500).
- NO random blur blobs without lighting purpose.
- NO ungrounded buzzwords ("Revolutionary", "Next-gen AI", "Seamlessly").
- NO generic 3-column cards with random Lucide icons in pastel circles.
- NO lazy TypeScript 'any'.
- NO missing active, hover, focus, or empty states.

# 3. CODE QUALITY
- Strict TypeScript: Full type definitions for all props, states, and API responses.
- Resilient error handling with clear user-facing messages.
- Lightweight, zero heavy npm animation bloat.
